💡 **SUGGESTION: the eager-navigation control flow is hard to follow**

The success/failure signal travels through mutation + re-read:

```dart
try {
  eager.location.href = authUrl.toString();
} on Object {
  // Fall through to the retry below.
  receiver?._popup = null;
}
if ((receiver?._popup) != null) {
  receiver?.trackPopup(eager);
  return;
}
```

The reader must simulate three states (navigated / threw / receiver null) to see
that `_popup != null` ⇔ "navigation succeeded". A local flag reads linearly:

```dart
var navigated = false;
try {
  eager.location.href = authUrl.toString();
  navigated = true;
} on Object {
  receiver?._popup = null; // window went away mid-flight — retry below
}
if (navigated) {
  receiver?.trackPopup(eager);
  return;
}
```

Behavior-identical, just easier to review the next time this file changes (which,
per the 404 incident, happens via hurried direct pushes). Optional.

